\label{sec:conclusion}

We present a framework for incorporating historical context into perception models with \name Map Priors (\oursbold), which employs a multi-resolution hash-based spatial encoding with binary quantization to efficiently store and retrieve prior spatial information.

Experiments on the nuScenes dataset demonstrate that \oursbold generalizes across diverse architectures, delivering consistent improvements with simple modifications to the architecture.
Our method is designed for environments where inference occurs in familiar, repeatedly traversed locations.
While CMP requires additional training for changing/completely new environments, the modular design enables efficient adaptation: the majority of model parameters (backbone, fusion modules, detector head) can be frozen while optimizing only the prior parameters for the new locations.

